  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The second term of a geometric sequence is $3$ and its fourth term is $27.$  Find the common ratio $r$ of this sequence given that $r$ is positive.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{4}=27$ and ${a}_{2}=3.$ Substituting $n=4$ and $m=2$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{4-2} & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{{a}_{2}} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{27}{3} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, solving the equation for $r$ and considering that $r$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {r}^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
